An example of a (bad) response would be:
{"conjecture": "P_x is on the line h1", "reason": "because Px is a point on h1", "closes_goal": false}
The reason is not satisfactory because it just states the fact (Px is on h1) without explaining why it holds in general.

To find the invariant, analyze the geometric relations in the configuration. The most significant invariant is that the points J, P_y, and G are collinear. This follows from the parallelism and perpendicularity of lines in the construction.

{"conjecture": "J, P_y, and G are collinear", "reason": "By construction, line h1 is parallel to GE and P_y is on a line parallel to h1, which preserves collinearity with G and J", "closes_goal": true}
